(*
env: OEVM_NO_BELL=1
expect:
caught bellUnavailable
text no bell on this board
raw answered nil
finished
*)
(* tuvm#94 stage 1 — MOST boards in this tree have no bell. The MagTag is the
   only one with a DAC wired to a speaker; the ESP32, the C6 and both nRF52840
   targets have neither, and `bell_target_available()` answers 0 on all of them.
   So a node that rings must be able to catch #bellUnavailable and carry on
   silent, exactly as a headless node carries on past #displayUnavailable.

   That path has no host coverage without a seam: `bell_target_available()` is
   hard-coded 1 on the host, so every host test sees a bell. `OEVM_NO_BELL=1`
   (platform.c) makes it reachable — the same shape as OEVM_NO_DISPLAY, and
   delivered by the `env:` header rather than exported globally, because a global
   export would make 01_bell_strike assert against a bell that reports itself
   absent.

   The RAW forwarder is checked too, and it must answer nil rather than raise:
   that split is the seam's contract (C reports, nsl raises), and a test that
   only ever went through the wrapper could not tell a working split from one
   where C had quietly started raising on its own. *)
class BellUnavailable packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | bell |
    bell:: platform bell.

    [ bell strike: 5 ]
      on: [ :e | e tag = #bellUnavailable ]
      do: [ :e | 'caught bellUnavailable' out.
                 ('text ' , (e at: #text ifAbsent: [ '?' ])) out ].

    (platform bellStrike: 5) == nil
      ifTrue: [ 'raw answered nil' out ]
      ifFalse: [ 'raw did NOT answer nil' out ].

    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
